EXTENSION "ArM5_Against_the_Dark_HiddenFortresses_NeculaiOfHouseBjornaer" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Against the Dark - Neculai of House Bjornaer"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_Against_the_Dark_Core_Ext"

    # Neculai of House Bjornaer (Chapter Seven: Networks of Hidden Fortresses, p103): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t793e61259baa3b4e3de907 ^"Neculai of House Bjornaer" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t1d5517e8227bc4dfca4b1d ^"Kezdö Válasz"]
            ^"Age" STRING "47 (apparent age: 39)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Observant +3, Agile +2, Grumpy +2. Privilege: Socius Neculai is a Hungarian native, born in the Carpathian foothills. Found by a migrating Bjornaer magus, he was apprenticed and raised in the Stonehenge Tribunal. Once gauntleted, he yearned for his homeland, and petitioned several Transylvanian covenants for membership. Needing an aedile at the time, Kezdö Válasz quickly accepted his application, to which he reluctantly agreed. Neculai is small-framed and hawkish, with a beak-like nose and hair so black that it seems tinted blue. An Intellego specialist, Neculai can magically speak to almost any bird, beast, and fish. Neculai is a member of Clan Sirnas, the branch of magi within House Bjornaer who serve as protectors and guardians. Always suspicious of House Tremere, and being one of the few non-Latin Houses of the Order, Clan Sirnas keeps a watchful eye on the Tremere magi. Neculai serves these interests well, and the clan expects him to return useful reports on the machinations of House Tremere. Personally, Neculai resents this role almost as much as he resents being paired with Adulio. He refuses to act covertly, either for his House or his oppidum sodales. He does not repeat what happens at the Gathering of Twelve Years to his oppidum members, but informs them that he may recount his personal observations at the Gathering, which he has twice attended since joining Kezdö Válasz. These observations may or may not contain Tremere business. Essedarius is unconcerned, saying that House Tremere has nothing to hide and House Bjornaer has nothing to fear. Neculai’s heartbeast is a pern, also called a honey buzzard: a kite-sized, migratory raptor that usually preys on wasp and hornet larva, but will also eat small reptiles, birds, and mammals. Flying is an ideal mode of transportation for the Tribunal’s rugged terrain. Recently, Essedarius has asked Neculai to visit Leona at the remote Prokletije fort, ostensibly to keep her informed of the oppidum’s business but also to keep her under observation."
            ^"Source" STRING "Against the Dark"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 103
        }
    }

}
